  "result": "Here's the everyday version, and I'm keeping it short.\n\nThink of a person sorting out a problem by texting a friend who has the answers. You text, \"Is the laser cutter free Friday?\" Your friend replies, \"Go check the booking calendar and tell me what it says.\" You look, then text back, \"Booked 2 to 4.\" Now your friend can answer: \"Then come at 5.\"\n\nSo the friend never looks at the calendar. They only ask for things and read what you send back. They repeat that until they can give you a real answer. That ask, result, ask again pattern is tool calling, and it's the loop you already traced for me.\n\nI'm stopping the analogy there on purpose. Quiz 0001 is still ungraded, and it asks about the details of this, like who does what and how the model picks a tool. If I mapped every part of the analogy to the real thing now, I'd be answering those items for you. Once it's graded, I'll give you the full version with real makerspace examples.\n\nFor now, try this: in the story above, who actually did the checking? Say what you think and why. I won't tell you if it's right yet, but it'll show us where it's fuzzy.",
